namespace gismo {

/** @defgroup Modules Runtime modules

The gsModules layer loads optional G+Smo modules as shared libraries at
runtime.

A module library exports two C-linkage entry points:

- \c gismo_module_info() returns a pointer to a gismo_module_info_t used
  for the ABI handshake: the module's ABI major version must equal the
  host's, its minor must not be newer, and its \c real_t / \c index_t
  type names must match the host exactly. Mismatching modules are
  rejected with a warning.
- \c gismo_module_register() populates the relevant gsRegistry (for
  example registering optimizer factories by name).

Modules are built with the \c gismo_add_module_lib() CMake function and
installed into \c lib/gismo/modules/ ; gsModuleManager::loadAll() scans
the \c GISMO_MODULE_DIR environment variable (if set) or the compiled-in
install location. Loaded libraries stay mapped for the process lifetime.

See gsRegistry, gsModuleManager and the gsModuleTemplate repository for
a worked example.
*/

}
